cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "如果这 105 行对你的工作有用，请按下面的格式引用。"
title: "Ganglion: a 105-line memory-backed verdict primitive"
abstract: >-
  A single-file, zero-dependency verdict primitive. One content in, three values out
  (1 pass / 0 problem / None undecided); a verdict already made within its TTL is not
  recomputed. Deliberately free of domain knowledge: it requires only a dict and a callable.
type: software
